  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agroecological circuits</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This amendment provides Taba with additional 18 months and $102,000 for the organization to reinforce its activities in support of smallholder farmers, including support for processing certified organic products, improving farmers? marketing strategies, and providing additional loans to smallholder farmers. Taba will also pilot a model of paid technical assistance. Finally, Taba will invest in strengthening the Povos da Mata sustainable agriculture network, bolster its participatory certification system, and expand activities to additional members of the network.</narrative>
  </description>
